    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-upside core, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Jackson Merrill** is our strongest play; he draws a favorable matchup against Pfaadt, and crucially, his score is bolstered by the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for **Jackson Merrill** to exploit his elite sprint speed in a league where stolen bases remain the primary scarcity. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a significant platoon advantage against McGreevy, with his projection surging thanks to a combination of SP skill and a move into the #3 hole, cementing him as a must-start in this Roto configuration.\n\nWhile **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.86) remains an elite volume producer, the rest of the lineup requires surgical management. **Kyle Tucker** (65.36) and **Andy Pages** (60.69) are solid starts against Matthew Boyd, though their scores are tempered by Boyd\u2019s efficiency at holding runners, which slightly caps their aggressive base-running potential. **Nasim Nunez** (50.95) represents our most marginal start; while his speed keeps him in the mix, the matchup against Nola is statistically unfavorable, and his lower spot in the order prevents him from climbing higher into the \"Strong\" tier.\n\nGiven the team-wide off-day for impact hitters like **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, the bench remains thin. **Jorge Polanco** and **Jordan Westburg** are unavailable due to scheduling and injury, respectively, leaving no viable candidates to challenge the current starting six for a spot. We are effectively playing our best available healthy options, accepting the lower efficiency scores on lower-order hitters to maintain our categorical pacing in a 5x5 format where every plate appearance is scrutinized against the daily game cap.",
